  "scope": "A bounded four-group source family is compiled by the existing compiler, runs two groups into distinct captured graphs, then saves the third Seq/All group at every collection frontier. Only host-owned bytes escape the initial execution. Decoded saved frames rebuild original captures and collectors and select a fourth group on a new host generation through existing native session APIs. Its operands depend on a restored atom, the second captured graph and the third group result. Numeric/text hosts cover 880 source/frontier/order combinations per owning or scope-bound raw session. Captured settled groups are not prepared or dispatched again; only unpublished third-group operands resume. Old replies fail both stale identity and current-identity/wrong-domain checks without consuming their allocation or fuel. Eight representative host/group combinations cover every remaining-fuel cutoff with owning/raw parity through final successor projection. Before-reentry denial, after-correlation revocation and explicit request cancellation stop before successor dispatch, seal the parent and reject later work. This is bounded host-owned byte recovery composition, not a production codec or journal, arbitrary source compatibility, crash settlement, cross-process exactly-once effects, complete language coverage or full extraction. Committed-byte provenance and already-performed side effects remain host responsibilities. No public API or contract version is added.",
